1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,020
Let me go ahead and open up Logos Bible Software.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:06,720
And let's begin with something very easy and something brand new.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:10,998
you may have already noticed it in the Logos window right here.

4
00:00:11,018 --> 00:00:13,770
And that little calendar icon

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:18,180
is to let you know that you have a reading plan associated with this book.

6
00:00:18,905 --> 00:00:19,690
And the nice shortcut

7
00:00:19,670 --> 00:00:26,510
about this is when you click on it, it goes to the next reading automatically and enables it so you

8
00:00:26,490 --> 00:00:30,441
know exactly what you have to read and where you are in the process.

9
00:00:30,522 --> 00:00:31,530
And of course, as you scroll

10
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:35,878
down and read the text, you also will see a Mark As Done button.

11
00:00:36,381 --> 00:00:37,870
And when you click that, you can

12
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:39,681
see now it moves you to Psalm 3.

13
00:00:40,063 --> 00:00:44,510
And so it'll keep track for you where your next read in that book

14
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:44,990
is.

15
00:00:44,731 --> 00:00:46,839
And that's such a helpful shortcut.
